"Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Aaron was able to run each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If Vanessa ran 4 miles and Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did vanessa take to complete her part?","Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Aaron was able to run each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If Vanessa ran 4 miles and Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Vanessa take to complete her part?",64,64,64,64,"Let Aaron’s speed be 2v (since he runs each mile twice as fast as Vanessa’s speed v), and let Aaron’s distance be d while Vanessa’s distance is 2d.

Given:
- Vanessa ran 4 miles, so 2d = 4 ⇒ d = 2 miles. Thus Aaron ran 2 miles.
- Aaron completed his part in 16 minutes.

Compute speeds:
- Aaron’s time = distance/speed ⇒ 16 minutes = 2 miles / (2v) hours (convert later).
But better to use consistent units:
Let v be in miles per minute for Vanessa. Then Aaron’s speed is 2v miles per minute.
Aaron’s time = distance/speed = 2 / (2v) = 1/v minutes.
Given 1/v = 16 ⇒ v = 1/16 miles per minute.

Vanessa’s time = distance/speed = 4 / v = 4 / (1/16) = 64 minutes.

