"Carlos is planting a lemon tree. The tree will cost $90 to plant. Each year it will grow 7 lemons, which he can sell for $1.5 each. It costs $3 a year to water and feed the tree. How many years will it take before he starts earning money on the LeMoN tree?","Carlos is planting a lemon tree. The tree will cost $90 to plant. Each year it will grow 7 lemons, which he can sell for $1.5 each. It costs $3 a year to water and feed the tree. How many years will it take before he starts earning money on the lemon tree?",13,13,12,13,"Let’s define variables:
- Initial planting cost: 90 dollars (one-time).
- Annual revenue from lemons: 7 lemons/year × 1.5 dollars/lemon = 10.5 dollars/year.
- Annual maintenance cost: 3 dollars/year.
- Net profit per year: 10.5 − 3 = 7.5 dollars/year.

We want the number of years n such that cumulative net earnings cover the initial cost:
7.5n ≥ 90
n ≥ 90 / 7.5 = 12

So it will take 12 years before he starts earning money (i.e., break even at 12, profit after that). #### 12",,"Let’s define variables:
