So it will take 12 years before he starts earning money (i.e., break even at 12, profit after that). #### 12","Let’s define variables:
- Initial cost to plant: $90 (one-time)
- Annual lemons: 7
- Price per lemon: $1.5
- Annual revenue: 7 × 1.5 = $10.5
- Annual maintenance cost: $3
- Annual net profit: 10.5 − 3 = $7.5

We want the number of years n until total profit exceeds the initial cost:
7.5n > 90

Solve for n:
n > 90 / 7.5 = 12

So after 12 years, he has exactly broken even. He starts earning money in the next year.

