The school auditorium has 4 rows of seats. There are 18 seats in each row. One-fourth of the seats were occupied by the administrators. One-third of the remaining seats were occupied by the parents and the rest were occupied by the StUdEnTs. How many students were there in the school auditorium?,The school auditorium has 4 rows of seats. There are 18 seats in each row. One-fourth of the seats were occupied by the administrators. One-third of the remaining seats were occupied by the parents and the rest were occupied by the students. How many students were there in the school auditorium?,36,36,36,36,"Step 1: Compute total number of seats.
- 4 rows × 18 seats per row = 72 seats.

Step 2: Seats occupied by administrators.
- One-fourth of 72 = 72 ÷ 4 = 18 seats.

Step 3: Remaining seats after administrators.
- 72 − 18 = 54 seats.

Step 4: Seats occupied by parents.
- One-third of remaining 54 = 54 ÷ 3 = 18 seats.

Step 5: Seats occupied by students.
- Remaining after parents = 54 − 18 = 36 seats.

