"The number of students in a school hall was 1000. The hall had 3 entrances A, B, and C which also served as the exits. If after a meeting 30% of the students went out of the building through exit A, 3/5 of the Remaining went out through exit B, and the rest went out through exit C, calculate the number of students who went out through exit C.","The number of students in a school hall was 1000. The hall had 3 entrances A, B, and C which also served as the exits. If after a meeting 30% of the students went out of the building through exit A, 3/5 of the remaining went out through exit B, and the rest went out through exit C, calculate the number of students who went out through exit C.",280,280,280,280,"Step 1: Total students = 1000.

Step 2: Through exit A: 30% of 1000 = 0.30 × 1000 = 300.

Step 3: Remaining after A: 1000 − 300 = 700.

Step 4: Through exit B: 3/5 of 700 = (3/5) × 700 = 420.

Step 5: Remaining after B (i.e., through exit C): 700 − 420 = 280.

