Ali has four $10 bills and six $20 bills that he saved after working for Mr. James on his farm. Ali gives her sister half of the total money he has and uses 3/5 of the remaining amount of money to buy Dinner. Calculate the amount of money he has after buying the dinner.,Ali has four $10 bills and six $20 bills that he saved after working for Mr. James on his farm. Ali gives her sister half of the total money he has and uses 3/5 of the remaining amount of money to buy dinner. Calculate the amount of money he has after buying the dinner.,32,32,32,32,"Step 1: Calculate Ali’s total money.
- Four $10 bills: 4 × 10 = 40
- Six $20 bills: 6 × 20 = 120
- Total = 40 + 120 = 160

Step 2: Ali gives his sister half of the total.
- Half of 160 = 160 ÷ 2 = 80
- Remaining = 160 − 80 = 80

Step 3: He uses 3/5 of the remaining to buy dinner.
- 3/5 of 80 = (3/5) × 80 = 48
- Money left after dinner = 80 − 48 = 32

